  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pillar 2 &#x2013; RBC Agreement for international responsible investment in the insurance sector, extra activities (extended)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) AgreementsThe Dutch government has concluded agreements on responsible business conduct (RBC) with Dutch sectors and civil society organisations. The agreements set out how companies can work with civil society organisations and government to prevent abuses in the areas of human rights, labour rights and the environment.Goal of this projectSupporting civil society organisations to make their knowledge available to play a role in the implementation of the RBC Agreement for international responsible investment in the insurance sector.The civil society organisations contribute to reduction of International Corporate Social Responsibility (ICSR) risks in international value chains conform their commitments, as set out in the RBC Agreement.NoteFVO&apos;s Pillar 2 projects support civil society organisations that make their knowledge of human rights due diligence and (international) network accessible to help achieve the goals of the ICSR covenants. Businesses, social organisations and government work together in ICSR covenants, to make value chains more sustainable. The covenants are organised by sector. The sectors have international value chains in multiple production countries/regions.RemarkDue to the transparency with regard to the IATI projects, a non-ODA country has been included in this project.More information: Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) agreementsUrl = https://www.imvoconvenanten.nl/en/insurance</narrative>
  </description>
